1 {Model Selection and Implementation}

To capture non-linear relationships and high-order interaction effects (e.g., severe storm penalties acting multiplicatively with heavy traffic congestion), a robust machine learning pipeline was implemented in Python using Scikit-Learn. A baseline Multiple Linear Regression model was deployed alongside a tuned Random Forest Regressor to validate the necessity of non-linear ensemble modeling.

